{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the page stream fallback at head 33540f977a4bc5d7ef00569f2b7d9ca9e665a2c9, tree 4b987b444745d414ddc09ee9408d9048deb0f1fe, for request 5874b15d and review request 7688f259. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED.\n\nThe head adds four commits to main 14ffb0f6 and changes 13 paths: the client observer and stream parser, the Page owner, data adapter, entry and assets, the Counter adapter, tests, `OBSERVE.md`, and the implementation note and its manifest. I read the implementation note first, then the source diff, the tests and the retained evidence. The design is right, and the served witness proves it. One defect in the settings loader needs a fix before landing.\n\n## Change requested\n\n1. An invalid stored `pollIntervalMs` disconnects the whole Page.\n   - `settings()` in `apps/room/page/src/main.ts:96` calls `pollingInterval(kept.pollIntervalMs)` inside its `try`. A stored value outside 1,000 to 60,000, or a string such as `\"5000\"`, throws a `RangeError`. The catch then returns `null`.\n   - Every caller treats `null` as a browser with no connection. The member's place, key and register become invisible. The member sees the entry screen.\n   - If the member then connects again, `saveSettings` in `browser-key-store.ts:62` replaces the stored record, because the record has not changed since it was read. The original connection record is gone. The private key stays in browser storage, but nothing points to it.\n   - The loader drops every other bad optional field on its own: `label`, `register` and `claimSelection`. `OBSERVE.md` documents `pollIntervalMs` as a retained setting that a person may set, so a typo reaches this path.\n   - Treat an invalid `pollIntervalMs` the same way: ignore it and use the 5,000 ms default, or show that the interval is invalid while keeping the connection. Add a Page test in which an invalid stored interval leaves `place` and `publicKey` readable.\n\n   The fix changes Page source outside the documents-only rule, so ruling 31962e1f needs one further full gate at the final head. The served-Page witness need not run again if the fix touches only the settings loader. The note should say why.\n\n## Against request 5874b15d\n\n1. Empty end of stream. Resolved. `headLines` throws `HeadStreamUnavailable` with reason `stream-ended-before-head` when a successful body ends before its first notice. The observer maps the error to `unavailable` and reports `fallback` once per outage. EOF after a notice reports `stream-ended`, and a session renewal reports `session-expired`.\n2. Backoff. Resolved. The default reconnect waits are 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 and then 30 seconds. `reconnectWait` makes the wait part of the observation lifetime instead of the read timeout. The first valid notice resets the failure count.\n3. Polling while unavailable. Resolved.\n   - `PageObservation` owns one observer for each view, keyed by settings context, route, interval and scope reference.\n   - It polls the complete authenticated summary only after a `fallback` state. It runs one read at a time, and each read is bounded by the interval.\n   - A `streaming` state stops polling and aborts the active read before another snapshot completes. Forbidden, unsupported, error and cancelled states also stop polling.\n   - `accept` refuses a different scope or definition, ignores an older head, and cancels on a hash conflict at the same sequence.\n4. Same-head restoration and stale paint. Resolved. The client emits `streaming` for a notice equal to the retained head. `current()` checks the owner, the lifetime and the binding after every await. The control that removes `stopPolling()` fails at `page-observation.test.ts:96`.\n5. Session and deployment. Resolved. `pageObservationSource` captures the first session's deployment, member, key and membership. A renewal replaces the shared Room reader only when all four match, and a mismatched poll supplies no snapshot. The note states that this is trust in the Page's own serving origin, not an independent pin.\n6. Sending fences. Resolved. Polls and notices trigger only redraws. No path in the diff submits an act, settles a pending request or changes custody.\n7. Counter. Resolved. Gate 1 failed because Counter's adapter rejected the new `streaming` state. Commit ce4cec64 makes the adapter ignore `streaming`, and gate 2 passes. Counter's app shows \"Connection unavailable\" for `fallback`, which is correct, because Counter does not poll.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 25930f62 gives a clean tree, 7b6eacdd.\n- Gate 2 checkpoint ce4cec64 has tree caa02206. Only the note and the manifest change from ce4cec64 to the head. From the witness checkpoint 0de86403 to ce4cec64, only `apps/counter/browser/client.ts` and its test change, so the served Page bytes of the Mac witness equal the head's.\n- I reran the owning files `apps/room/page/test/page-observation.test.ts` and `packages/client/test/observe.test.ts` once, with no whole suite. They pass 24 of 24 tests. The Counter owner runs under its own runner, and I took its result from gate 2 and `counter-owning-1`.\n- The manifest has SHA-256 dda3ad07 and 45,384 bytes. It follows ruling 4e199bd8:\n  - all 280 listed files match by size and SHA-256;\n  - `finalization` and `operator-inputs` match their digests, and each SHA256SUMS reruns clean, with no unlisted file;\n  - the root SHA256SUMS covers all 1,913 other files, with none unlisted and none writable.\n- The served witness `mac-two-browser-polling-2` records one sender POST and none from the receiver. The receiver shows the comment after 5,348.97 ms, within two 5-second intervals. Both browsers exit 0. The DNS rule and the endpoint-certificate exception apply only to the browser and are stated. The configured-register 403s come from the optional founding-offer read at `main.ts:968-974`, and the helper accepts only that endpoint and status, with matching counts.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 743 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from 14ffb0f6: one warning, for the 45,384-byte manifest over the 40,960-byte soft limit, as disclosed.\n- check-commit-messages from 14ffb0f6: 4 checked, 0 flagged.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The note names Chromium. \"A headed browser\" says the same thing within the naming rule.\n2. The healthy-stream case, a working stream with no polls, has only the scripted owning test. The note says so. A native trial can wait for a celld version that delivers notices.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe fallback sits entirely in the client and the Page. It adds two local observation states and a view-lifetime owner. It changes no native definition, kernel, Worker route, stream wire or session rule. The signed-request and authenticated-read contract in `docs/architecture.md` holds, and `OBSERVE.md` records the new local states. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\n- Polls use the same authenticated summary read as the initial draw. A renewed session must match the captured deployment, member, key and membership before it replaces the shared reader.\n- No observation state or diagnostic reason carries a token or key.\n- Item 1 is a custody risk. A bad optional value hides the member's stored connection and invites them to overwrite it.\n\nApproved, subject to item 1.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe owner is 117 lines, and it reuses the observer's existing states instead of adding a second reader. Polling runs only during an outage and stops on the first notice. The Counter repair is one guard. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved, subject to item 1.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: the fallback, backoff, serialized polling, same-head restoration, retirement, session checks, stale-paint suppression and sending fences hold in the source, the tests, the controls and the served witness. Item 1 needs a fix and one further gate.\n\nA head that makes item 1 can come back for a short review of the diff.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4d3a60cce74f0e6f845bf7a66cb12dfc148341a8","binding":"assigned","head":"33540f977a4bc5d7ef00569f2b7d9ca9e665a2c9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2c571d099d84dd9cd53a42c50d8e9f40b0ece651\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:987563d7f9393ff6fc42aa477925bef2f78e5f24\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2c571d099d84dd9cd53a42c50d8e9f40b0ece651","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}